.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_FORMAT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_FORMAT \- A variable controlling the default audio format.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_FORMAT \(dqSDL_AUDIO_FORMAT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the application doesn\(aqt specify the audio format when opening the device, this hint can be used to specify a default format that will be used\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqU8\(dq: Unsigned 8-bit audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqS8\(dq: Signed 8-bit audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqS16LE\(dq: Signed 16-bit little-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqS16BE\(dq: Signed 16-bit big-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqS16\(dq: Signed 16-bit native-endian audio (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dqS32LE\(dq: Signed 32-bit little-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqS32BE\(dq: Signed 32-bit big-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqS32\(dq: Signed 32-bit native-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqF32LE\(dq: Floating point little-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqF32BE\(dq: Floating point big-endian audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqF32\(dq: Floating point native-endian audio
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

